(vector (map (:adr/related (vector "2607071250-cloud-itonami-brokerage-6612-coverage" "2607071320-cloud-itonami-credit-6492-coverage" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage" "2607071618-cloud-itonami-marketadmin-6611-coverage" "2607071640-cloud-itonami-testlab-7120-coverage" "2607071654-cloud-itonami-clinic-8620-coverage" "2607071717-cloud-itonami-registrar-8530-coverage" "2607071732-cloud-itonami-wagering-9200-coverage" "2607071752-cloud-itonami-veterinary-7500-coverage" "2607071819-cloud-itonami-funeral-9603-coverage" "2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607071922-cloud-itonami-parksafety-9321-coverage" "2607072715-cloud-itonami-eldercare-8730-coverage" "2607072730-cloud-itonami-museum-9102-coverage" "2607072745-cloud-itonami-conservation-9103-coverage" "2607072800-cloud-itonami-salon-9602-coverage" "2607072815-cloud-itonami-entertainment-9000-coverage" "2607072830-cloud-itonami-casework-8890-coverage" "2607072845-cloud-itonami-hospital-8610-coverage" "2607072900-cloud-itonami-facility-9311-coverage" "2607072915-cloud-itonami-school-8510-coverage" "2607080100-cloud-itonami-association-9412-coverage" "2607080200-cloud-itonami-leasing-6491-coverage" "2607080300-cloud-itonami-behavioral-8720-coverage" "2607080400-cloud-itonami-secondary-8521-coverage" "2607080500-cloud-itonami-card-6619-coverage" "2607080600-cloud-itonami-water-3600-coverage" "2607080700-cloud-itonami-telecom-6190-coverage" "2607080800-cloud-itonami-aerospace-3030-coverage" "2607080900-cloud-itonami-recovery-3830-coverage" "2607081000-cloud-itonami-consulting-7020-coverage" "2607081100-cloud-itonami-union-9420-coverage" "2607081200-cloud-itonami-congregation-9491-coverage" "2607081300-cloud-itonami-fab-2610-coverage" "2607081400-cloud-itonami-energy-3512-coverage" "2607081500-cloud-itonami-care-8810-coverage" "2607081600-cloud-itonami-navigator-8691-coverage" "2607081700-cloud-itonami-learning-8569-coverage" "2607081800-cloud-itonami-banking-6419-coverage" "2607081900-cloud-itonami-advertising-7310-coverage" "2607082100-cloud-itonami-polling-7320-coverage" "2607082200-cloud-itonami-research-7210-coverage" "2607082300-cloud-itonami-design-7410-coverage" "2607082600-cloud-itonami-nursing-8710-coverage" "2607082800-cloud-itonami-sports-8541-coverage" "2607082900-cloud-itonami-alliedhealth-8690-coverage" "2607083000-cloud-itonami-laundry-9601-coverage" "2607083300-cloud-itonami-holdco-6420-coverage" "2607083500-cloud-itonami-photo-7420-coverage" "2607083600-cloud-itonami-personalservice-9609-coverage" "2607083800-cloud-itonami-edsupport-8550-coverage" "2607084000-cloud-itonami-headoffice-7010-coverage" "2607084300-cloud-itonami-residential-8790-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic- ADR-0001s" "langgraph ADR-0001")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "2607084400"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 67, :blueprint 17, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/test-status-8542 "30 tests / 132 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean single-actuation lifecycle plus four HARD-hold cases); kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 116 assertions, all green, no pre-existing fixture referenced ISIC \"8542\""), (:adr/distinctive-check-8542 "child-performer-work-permit-unresolved-violations is a GENUINELY NEW concept (grep-verified absent -- zero hits for 'child-performer'/'performer-license'/'entertainment-work-permit' across every prior sibling), the 53rd distinct application of the unconditional-evaluation discipline overall (casualty.governor/sanctions-violations's original fix; most recently residential.governor/background-check-not-cleared-violations at 52nd), grounded in real child-performer labor law: California Labor Code section 1308.5, UK's Children (Performances and Activities) Regulations 2014, Japan's Labor Standards Act Article 56/57, Germany's JArbSchG section 6"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607084400: `cloud-itonami-isic-8542` (cultural education) deepened to `:implemented`\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted.\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607032000 (original insurance/real-estate batch)\n- ADR-2607084000 (`cloud-itonami-isic-7010`, activities of head offices)\n- ADR-2607084300 (`cloud-itonami-isic-8790`, other residential care activities)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-8542/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (child-repo architecture ADR)\n- `langgraph` ADR-0001 (StateGraph actor pattern)\n\n## Context\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-8542` publishes an OSS business blueprint for\ncultural education: instruction in music, arts, dance, language and\nother cultural skills. Like every prior vertical in this fleet, the\nblueprint text alone is not an implementation — this ADR records the\ngoverned-actor build that promotes `cloud-itonami-isic-8542` from\n`:blueprint` to `:implemented` in the `kotoba-lang/industry`\nregistry, the fifty-fourth vertical built outside ADR-2607032000's\noriginal insurance/real-estate batch.\n\n## Problem\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-isic-8542`'s blueprint described a real-world\n   cultural-education operating model (student intake, curriculum\n   verification, certification/progress-record finalization) but had\n   no governed-actor implementation: no Store, no Governor, no\n   rollout phasing, no tests.\n2. The blueprint's own text names only ONE real-world act\n   (\"finalizing a certification or progress record\") — this build\n   needed the single-actuation shape.\n3. Cultural education (music, arts, dance) frequently involves minors\n   performing in public/recorded settings, which carries a genuine,\n   real-world compliance concern distinct from every prior sibling:\n   child-performer work-permit law (distinct from generic guardian\n   consent, distinct from staff background checks) — no dedicated\n   check for this concept exists anywhere else in this fleet.\n4. This fleet already has an \"hours completed vs. hours required\"\n   concept (`secondary`/8521's attendance-hours-insufficient?) — this\n   build's own practice-hours check needed to honestly characterize\n   its own reuse rather than overclaim novelty.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Single-actuation shape.** Following `sports`/8541's precedent for\n   resolving the same either/or-naming ambiguity, \"certification or\n   progress record\" is treated as ONE conceptual act. Matching\n   `leasing`/`underwriting`/`testlab`/`clinic`/`veterinary`/`funeral`/\n   `parksafety`/`salon`/`entertainment`/`facility`/`consulting`/\n   `advertising`/`polling`/`research`/`design`/`sports`/`alliedhealth`/\n   `photo`/`personalservice`/`edsupport`'s single-actuation shape,\n   `high-stakes` is the one-member set `#{:actuation/finalize-\n   certification}`.\n2. **Entity and op shape.** Primary entity `student`. Four ops:\n   `:student/intake`, `:curriculum/verify`, `:permit/screen`,\n   `:actuation/finalize-certification` (high-stakes).\n3. **`child-performer-work-permit-unresolved-violations` — the 53rd\n   unconditional-evaluation grounding, a genuinely new concept.**\n   Grep-verified absent (zero hits for \"child-performer\"/\"performer-\n   license\"/\"entertainment-work-permit\" across every prior sibling).\n   Grounded in California Labor Code §1308.5, UK's Children\n   (Performances and Activities) Regulations 2014, Japan's Labor\n   Standards Act Article 56/57, and Germany's JArbSchG §6. Gates\n   `:permit/screen` and the actuation.\n4. **`practice-hours-insufficient?` — an honest ninth MINIMUM-\n   threshold instance, not claimed as new.** Directly analogous to\n   `secondary.registry/attendance-hours-insufficient?`'s own shape.\n   Gates only the actuation (a pure ground-truth recompute, no\n   dedicated screening op needed).\n5. **Dedicated double-actuation-guard boolean.** `:certification-\n   finalized?` on the `student` record, never a single `:status`\n   value.\n6. **Store protocol, MemStore + DatomicStore parity**, proven via\n   `test/cultural/store_contract_test.clj`. The per-entity accessor\n   is safely named `student` directly.\n7. **Phase 0→3 rollout** — Phase 3's `:auto` set is `{:student/\n   intake}` only; the actuation is permanently excluded from every\n   phase's `:auto` set.\n8. **No bespoke domain capability lib** — this blueprint's own\n   `:itonami.blueprint/required-technologies` names no domain-\n   specific capability beyond the generic stack.\n9. **Mock + LLM advisor pair** — `mock-advisor` default everywhere,\n   `llm-advisor` with a defensive EDN-proposal parser.\n10. **No `blueprint.edn` field-sync fixes needed** — the `isic-`\n    prefixed `:id` and `:required-technologies`/`:optional-\n    technologies` already matched the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry\n    exactly; only the `:maturity` field itself needed adding.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Sixty-eighth actor in this fleet (67 implemented before this\n  build).\n- Establishes a genuinely NEW unconditional-evaluation-screening\n  concept (child-performer-work-permit-unresolved), grep-verified\n  absent from every prior sibling before the claim was finalized.\n- Documents an honest NINTH instance of the MINIMUM-threshold\n  sufficiency check family, not claimed as new.\n- `MemStore` ‖ `DatomicStore` parity is proven by `test/cultural/\n  store_contract_test.clj`.\n- Fleet maturity: `:implemented` 67 → 68, `:blueprint` 17 → 16,\n  `:spec` 546 unchanged, total 643.\n- Test status: 30 tests / 132 assertions, lint clean, demo verified\n  end-to-end.\n- `kotoba-lang/industry`'s full test suite re-run with the local-root\n  `technology` override before committing — 7 tests / 116 assertions,\n  all green, no pre-existing fixture referenced ISIC \"8542\".\n- This build's `deps.edn` used the CURRENT `kotoba-lang/langgraph`/\n  `langchain` coordinates from the start (see `holdco`/6420's own\n  ADR-0001 for the upstream-rename context this build inherited).\n- Next vertical selection remains unconstrained under the standing\n  authorization.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|---|---|\n| A dual-actuation shape (certification + progress record as two acts) | The blueprint's own text consistently names only ONE real-world act; following `sports`/8541's precedent, the either/or naming is treated as one conceptual act |\n| Reusing `photo`/7420's `minor-subject-guardian-consent-unresolved?` concept | Guardian consent (parental consent for image use) and a child-performer work permit (labor-authority authorization to perform/work) are distinct real-world regulatory regimes — consent law vs. child-labor law |\n| Reusing `secondary`/8521's `attendance-hours-insufficient?` literally without renaming | A domain-appropriate rename (`practice-hours-insufficient?`) better fits this vertical's own vocabulary, while the reuse is honestly documented, matching `holdco`/6420's \"reused, renamed for domain fit\" precedent |\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8542/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8542/README.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-8542/docs/business-model.md`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (entry `\"8542\"`)"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 68, :blueprint 16, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/blueprint-already-correct-8542 "this repo's blueprint.edn already had the correct isic- prefixed :id and correctly populated :required-technologies/:optional-technologies matching the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"8542\" exactly -- only the :maturity field itself needed adding"), (:adr/deps-edn-current-coordinates-from-start-8542 "this build's deps.edn used the CURRENT io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph + langchain coordinates and :local/root paths from the very start, inheriting the fix holdco/6420's build discovered and documented -- see holdco/6420's own ADR-0001 for the full upstream-rename context (a repo transfer + rename, internal namespaces unchanged)"), (:adr/no-bespoke-capability-lib-8542 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies names no domain-specific capability beyond the generic robotics/identity/forms/dmn/bpmn/audit-ledger stack -- there was no capability-lib decision to make at all"), (:adr/pattern-8542 "sealed StudioEdOps-LLM + independent Instruction Integrity Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all sixty-seven prior actors; FIFTY-FOURTH build outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch (after 6612, 6492, 6920, 6611, 7120, 8620, 8530, 9200, 7500, 9603, 9521, 9321, 8730, 9102, 9103, 9602, 9000, 8890, 8610, 9311, 8510, 9412, 6491, 8720, 8521, 6619, 3600, 6190, 3030, 3830, 7020, 9420, 9491, 2610, 3512, 8810, 8691, 8569, 6419, 7310, 7320, 7210, 7410, 8710, 8541, 8690, 9601, 6420, 7420, 9609, 8550, 7010, 8790)"), (:adr/date "2026-07-08"), (:adr/single-actuation-8542 "this blueprint's own README/business-model.md/operator-guide.md text consistently names only ONE real-world act (finalizing a certification or progress record), following sports/8541's either/or-naming precedent, so this build uses the single-actuation shape (#{:actuation/finalize-certification})"), (:adr/scope-note "this is a NEW ADR because ISIC 8542 (cultural education) contributes a genuinely new check concept (child-performer-work-permit-unresolved?) despite reusing an existing check-family shape for its second distinctive check, warranting its own record per this fleet's standing per-vertical-ADR convention"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/honest-reuse-check-8542 "practice-hours-insufficient? is an honest NINTH instance of this fleet's MINIMUM-threshold sufficiency check family (veterinary/funeral/hospital established the first three temporal instances, association/secondary/polling/research generalized it to non-temporal as the fourth through seventh, personalservice's cooling-off-period-not-elapsed? returned to temporal as the eighth), directly analogous to secondary.registry/attendance-hours-insufficient?'s own hours-completed/hours-required shape, not claimed as new"), (:adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-8542"), (:adr/lesson-applied-proactively-8542 "tested via :permit/screen directly from the start (not via an actuation op against an unscreened student), applying parksafety's ADR-2607071922 Decision 5 / eldercare's, museum's, conservation's, salon's, entertainment's, casework's, hospital's, facility's, school's, association's, leasing's, behavioral's, secondary's, card's, water's, telecom's, aerospace's, recovery's, consulting's, union's, congregation's, fab's, energy's, care's, navigator's, learning's, banking's, advertising's, polling's, research's, design's, nursing's, sports's, alliedhealth's, laundry's, holdco's, photo's, personalservice's, edsupport's, headoffice's and residential's ADR-0001 lesson PROACTIVELY for a forty-first consecutive vertical"), (:adr/no-dedicated-screening-op-for-reuse-8542 "practice-hours-insufficient-violations gates only the actuation (a pure ground-truth recompute, no dedicated screening op needed, matching secondary/8521's own scoping) -- only the genuinely new child-performer-permit concept has a dedicated screening op (:permit/screen)"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-8542 (cultural education) deepened to :implemented -- fifty-fourth vertical outside the original batch"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))